<title>UK: Algeria raises LPG prices by up to $50 a tonne.</title>
<headline>Algeria raises LPG prices by up to $50 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil company Sonatrach said it had raised its official prices for liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) for October by up to $50 a tonne.</p>
<p>The price for propane loading at Bethioua will be $240 a tonne, up from $190 in September.</p>
<p>Butane will be $230 a tonne, up from $195 in September.</p>
<p>LPG loading at Skikda will be $7 a tonne over the Bethioua price.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
